/target/

# The demo consumes the extension through a render-time copy of
# extensions/vertext (Quarto's extension discovery does not follow symlinks),
# so the repository keeps exactly one copy of the filter and stylesheet.
# Run examples/render.sh to produce this directory.
#
# This rule was written before the files it names were untracked, so it did
# nothing for three weeks: git applies .gitignore to untracked paths only, and
# `git check-ignore` answers for a tracked path as though the rule were absent.
# A rule added after the fact needs `git rm --cached` in the same commit or it
# is decoration.
/examples/_extensions/

# Soulstem session config — persona stays out of the repository.
/.claude/

# `quarto render` output. The rendered page and its support directory are
# derived from examples/quarto-demo.qmd and the extension, and the support
# directory is mostly third-party: bootstrap, bootstrap-icons, popper, tippy,
# clipboard and anchor arrived minified, unlicensed and unattributed, ~850KB of
# it. Nothing in the repository reads either path — no test, no script, no
# document links to them — so they were weight and a licence question, not a
# fixture. Run examples/render.sh to produce them.
/examples/quarto-demo.html
/examples/quarto-demo_files/
